<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  macOS asks before an app may see through a camera, and it refuses to ask at
  all unless the app has said why in its own bundle. Without this key
  `getUserMedia` does not prompt and does not fail with a message — the app
  is killed, which is the worst of the three outcomes and the one nobody can
  debug from a bug report.

  Tauri merges this file into the bundle's generated Info.plist at build time,
  so it holds only what the generator does not already write.

  The sentence is the one a macOS dialog puts after "Yames would like to access
  the camera", so it is written the way every other promise in this app is
  written: what it is for, and where it goes. `plans/WEBSITE_DECISIONS.md` —
  the reader is a musician, never a developer.

  No microphone key, deliberately, and it must stay that way: the webview never
  opens a microphone. The sound of a take is the engine's, recorded through
  cpal on its own threads (`src-tauri/src/take.rs`), and adding
  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription here would tell macOS to offer a permission this
  app's webview has no code to ask for.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Yames records you playing, so you can watch it back beside the notes. The recording is kept on this Mac and is never uploaded.</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
